Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:03.74,Default,,0,0,0,,At 52, she wasn't afraid of being alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.74,0:00:06.56,Default,,0,0,0,,She was afraid of {\c&H99E5FF&\b1}choosing wrong again{\c&HFFFFFF&\b1}.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.56,0:00:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,After a painful relationship, even a kind invitation felt risky.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.00,0:00:14.75,Default,,0,0,0,,When someone asked her to dinner, she nearly said no—
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.75,0:00:19.52,Default,,0,0,0,,not because she didn't want love,\Nbut because she remembered the cost.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.52,0:00:21.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Then she asked herself:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.97,0:00:26.02,Default,,0,0,0,,"What if protecting my heart\Nmeans never giving it a chance?"
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.02,0:00:28.60,Default,,0,0,0,,She didn't promise herself a happy ending.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.60,0:00:31.04,Default,,0,0,0,,She said yes to {\c&H99E5FF&\b1}one coffee{\c&HFFFFFF&\b1}.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.04,0:00:34.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Because starting over doesn't mean trusting everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.20,0:00:37.81,Default,,0,0,0,,It means learning from the past\Nwithout letting it choose {\c&H99E5FF&\b1}your future{\c&HFFFFFF&\b1}.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.30,0:00:10.50,Message,,0,0,0,,Would you like to get dinner this Friday?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.30,0:00:40.00,FinalQ,,0,0,0,,Would you give love another chance?
